From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: quote list-valued cache variable in root-config generation

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/root-project/root/commit/227e0753f5c5ef9070b892d70848192fc16d06d5]

The loop that populates ROOT_CONFIGARGS dereferences every cache
variable unquoted, `NOT ${${var}} STREQUAL ""`, so a cache variable
holding a list expands into several if() arguments. CMake 4.4 adds the
list-valued CMAKE_DIAGNOSTIC_INIT cache variable (set from the
`-Wno-dev` setup.py passes) and, unlike CMake 3.x, which ignored the
stray arguments, rejects them before the leading `var MATCHES` test can
rule the variable out, so configure aborts with "Unknown arguments
specified". Quote the value, as ROOT
itself now does; the cppyy-backend copy of this top-level CMakeLists.txt
was forked from ROOT before the fix.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 cling/src/CMakeLists.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/cling/src/CMakeLists.txt b/cling/src/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/cling/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/cling/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -187,7 +187,7 @@ include(SearchInstalledSoftware)
 get_cmake_property(variables CACHE_VARIABLES)
 foreach(var ${variables})
   if((var MATCHES "_(LIBRARIES|LIBRARY|INCLUDE|VERSION)") AND
-     (NOT ${${var}} STREQUAL "") AND
+     (NOT "${${var}}" STREQUAL "") AND
      (NOT ${var} MATCHES "NOTFOUND"))
     if (var MATCHES "^QT_")
       # filter out the very long list of Qt libraries and include dirs
